  "conclusions": [
    "The native one-percent BlockFHT c_proj generator tangent has substantial task-conditioned functional capacity: it explains 60.28 percent of held-out matched endpoint correction energy, about 13.94 times the fixed random rank-64 full-core span.",
    "The capacity is not local in the trained coordinates. Full coverage requires a mean fitted displacement 1.21 times the entire trained latent norm; even the four-iteration solution already crosses 1.05 times that norm.",
    "At a more local 0.46-times-trained-latent displacement, held-out explained energy is only 35.60 percent. The fit/holdout gap at convergence is modest, so the result is not primarily sample-window overfitting.",
    "The plain c_proj run was configured as Muon, but its one-dimensional BlockFHT latents were actually optimized by the AdamW fallback at 0.3 times the main learning rate, or 7.2e-4. The earlier Muon conclusions apply to matrix add-ons, not to the native generator latents.",
    "This rejects the simple claim that c_proj fails because its native generator manifold lacks useful directions. The stronger diagnosis is a nonlocal, poorly conditioned exploration problem in generator coordinates.",
    "The endpoint target compares separately co-adapted models and the per-layer fits are independent. It does not prove that one simultaneous latent update recovers network validation loss."
  ],
